==Enemy==
He has a long-ranged Area Attack with a 30% chance to warp Cats backwards by 250 range and is protected by an extremely weak [[Barrier]]. Thankfully, he's much weaker than his [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] [[Mr. Mole|counterpart]] due to his lower stats and attack rate, plus having a trait making him vulnerable to any [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien Cats]].

==Strategy==
If Corporal Weyland has no backup, it's a simple task to defeat him, since his standing range is equivalent to his minimum range and his Barrier is rather fragile. If he has backup, then he can be slightly problematic, as he can teleport groups of cats from a distance. The only caveat is that he has low attack power compared to other Starred Alien enemies, so usually he shouldn't pose a threat.

Corporal Weyland's greatest asset is that he can constantly warp your longer-ranged slow-attacking units, making them nearly unusable. But because of his rather low HP for a backliner, he is highly susceptible to being sniped by [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] cats, and is directly countered by [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat]]. [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] (particularly [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahumut Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]) also work well against him, as they have shorter range, and can therefore creep into his blind spot, destroying him before he could hit them.

